  "grammar": {
    "title": "Verbs in -ir like finir (2nd group)",
    "intro": "Verbs of the 2nd group end in -ir and add -iss- in the plural. They are all regular: learn finir and you know choisir, réussir, réfléchir, grandir…",
    "table": [
      [
        "",
        "finir",
        "choisir"
      ],
      [
        "je",
        "finis",
        "choisis"
      ],
      [
        "tu",
        "finis",
        "choisis"
      ],
      [
        "il / elle",
        "finit",
        "choisit"
      ],
      [
        "nous",
        "finissons",
        "choisissons"
      ],
      [
        "vous",
        "finissez",
        "choisissez"
      ],
      [
        "ils / elles",
        "finissent",
        "choisissent"
      ]
    ],
    "examples": [
      {
        "fr": "Je finis à quinze heures.",
        "en": "I finish at 3 pm."
      },
      {
        "fr": "Nous choisissons nos horaires.",
        "en": "We choose our hours."
      },
      {
        "fr": "Tu réfléchis trop !",
        "en": "You think too much!"
      }
    ],
    "trap": "finis, finis, finit all sound the same. In the plural you hear -iss-: « ils finissent ». Not every -ir verb works like this: partir, sortir, dormir and venir are irregular (nous partons, not « partissons »)."
  },
  "sounds": {
    "title": "t or d?",
    "explain": "Like p / b: t is crisp, d vibrates. At the end of a word, French pronounces them clearly when they are followed by -e: « verte », « grande ».",
